+# archive (s-ui-linux-amd64.tar.gz) plus SHA256SUMS from the GitHub Release,
+# and it resolves the version through releases/latest.
+#
+# That last detail is what makes the upstream triggers actively harmful. The
+# publish job marks its release `prerelease: true`, and releases/latest skips
+# prereleases -- so a tag-triggered run would hide the release we published by
+# hand and send install.sh back to the previous version, silently. It would
+# also spend an hour building seven platforms, two of which need the Chromium
+# toolchain, for archives nobody downloads.
+#
+# Keep the workflow for a deliberate manual run; let the release be published
+# from the built artifact instead.
